Snake Game

A modern take on the classic Snake arcade game written entirely in Java Swing. Choose your difficulty, dodge randomly‑placed obstacles, and chase special power‑up food while trying to set a new high score!

## Features

 Gameplay 

 Details 

Difficulty Selector

Easy (150 ms), Medium (100 ms), Hard (50 ms) game‑loop speeds picked via a startup dialog.

Random Obstacles

Ten static obstacles spawn each round, forcing you to plan your path.

Power‑Up Food

Every 5th snack is a blue 2×2 mega‑fruit worth +5 points.

Pause & Resume

Press P to freeze the action. A centered overlay reminds you you’re paused.

Persistent High Score

Your best run is saved in highscore.txt and displayed on‑screen.

Instant Restart

Hit Space after Game Over to dive straight back in.

## Controls

 Key 

 Action 

← ↑ → ↓

Move snake (no reverse into yourself!)

P

Pause / Resume

Space

Restart after Game Over

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

Java 8 JDK or newer (no external libraries needed).

### Build & Run

# Clone the repo
$ git clone https://github.com/HassanRasheed91/Snake-Game.git
$ cd Snake-Game

# Compile
$ javac Game.java SnakeGame.java

# Launch
$ java Game

Tip: package the two .class files into a JAR for one‑click launching.

## Project Structure

Snake-Game/
├── Game.java          # Program entry‑point & difficulty dialog
├── SnakeGame.java     # Core game logic, rendering & input handling
└── highscore.txt      # Auto‑created; stores top score across sessions

## Customization

Board Size — change boardWidth in Game.java (height follows automatically).

Obstacle Count — edit placeObstacles() in SnakeGame.java.

Speed Tuning — tweak the millisecond delay passed to the Timer constructor.

## Screenshots / GIFs
Add a docs/ folder with gameplay images or record a GIF with an open‑source screen‑recorder to show the game in action.

## Contributing
Pull requests are welcome. If you find a bug or have an idea for a new feature, please open an issue first so we can discuss it.

